AS DELIVERED
Thank you Chair and thank you to the ECOSOC President for convening today’s important discussion on Haiti. And thank you to the panelists for sharing your insights and bringing us up-to-date information on the situation in Haiti.
Colleagues, the security situation in Haiti remains dire, especially in Port-au-Prince. Gang violence affects the daily lives of the Haitian people.
We commend the extraordinary bravery of the Haitian National Police, and all international personnel supporting the MSS mission, for their work to establish stability and security in the country.
However, more is needed. The MSS mission is at a critical juncture, and additional funding and equipment are urgently required.
Now more than ever, coordination and cohesion across the Haitian government is sorely needed to fight the criminal gangs terrorizing the Haitian people. These gangs are responsible for widespread violence and instability, including attacks on civilians and law enforcement.
Gang control of key routes and infrastructure hinders the flow of goods and damages livelihoods through extortion and limiting access to resources. Urgent action is required.
Recently, some gang leaders have vocalized their ambitions to seize control of the government and have used increasingly brutal tactics against civilians to achieve this objective.
This is why the United States has designated a prominent Haitian gang and gang coalition, Viv Ansanm and Gran Grif, as Foreign Terrorist Organizations and Specially Designated Global Terrorists. This action restricts gang members’ access to the U.S. financial system and material support that could support their activities, such as gun trafficking.
We urge Haiti’s leaders to prioritize the security of the Haitian people, support anti-corruption efforts, promote accountability for those responsible for abuses, and end impunity for violence against civilians.
The United States will continue to work closely with the Organization of American States, the MSS mission, the Haitian government, BINUH, and other international partners to bring an end to this unnecessary crisis and senseless loss of human life. Thank you.
