The United States thanks Mongolia for its leadership and efforts in facilitating the process on this resolution.
The United States also appreciates the efforts by several members to seek compromise throughout the negotiation, including to remove preambular climate references that distracted from the true matter under consideration.
However, the text of this resolution contains positions we cannot support, which compels us to call the vote today.
Regrettably, there were no textual accommodations in support of consensus, despite initial flexibility during open negotiations, regarding preambular language on the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development and the Sustainable Development Goals.
The United States has made clear that the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development and the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) impinge upon state sovereignty as a soft form of global governance, and we will no longer reaffirm them as a matter of course in UN resolutions.
For these reasons, the United States will call a vote on this resolution.
Thank you.
